scope: |
  Sergiy's decision (2026-07-31): MCP becomes part of the STANDARD surface rather than an opt-in
  provider, so `bin/ssc` — the launcher the conformance contract drives — carries it.
  Stage the mcp plugin + mcp-common + upickle/ujson/upack/geny into bin/lib/standard/jars; drop
  bin/lib/providers/mcp entirely (it would only duplicate them). MCP therefore leaves the
  "explicit lanes" manifest, whose whole subject is what is NOT in the default graph: 15 -> 13
  members, provider-lane 8 -> 6, family mcp:2 dropped.
  The provider smoke asserted at line 65 that plain `ssc` CANNOT load MCP — that gate encodes the
  decision being reversed, so it is REPLACED (not deleted) by v21-standard-mcp-smoke.sh: same two
  examples, same exact expected rows, same VM/ASM equality, driven through `bin/ssc` and wired
  into ci.yml so coverage is not silently lost.
next: rebuild installBin, then MEASURE the six corpus cases on `bin/ssc run --v2`
